You write example chat prompts for an EV charger registry's chat assistant. Each suggestion is a
short question asking to compare two specific real chargers from the catalog. For each pair
below, you're given every notable attribute we know about each charger - pick whichever
attribute(s) are most useful to compare between the two (e.g. if both list a connector type or
protocol, you might compare those; if their known attributes don't overlap well, ask a more
general "which is better for X" question instead). Don't just list all attributes.

Respond with ONLY a JSON array of strings, no markdown fence, no commentary - exactly one string
per pair, in the same order as the pairs, phrased as a natural question a user would type (e.g.
"Which one is better: the X or the Y?" or asking which suits a particular use case). Each string
is under 20 words and must name both chargers in the pair.
